WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.080
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.750
But it's not enough.  I’m sorry.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.640
No, you fought excellently.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.560
I’m proud to be your partner.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.060
Thank you, Aqua.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.110
This is my compassion.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.280
Aoi!

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.480
Brother?

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.780
Aoi!

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:35.010
Brother…

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.610
Aoi!

00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:01.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:08.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:15.430
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:22.000
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.980
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:42.690
I want to share your pain

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:18.190
Blue Maiden and Aqua, come with me!

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.230
Blue Maiden lost!

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.730
Let’s get her revenge together!

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.710
You…

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.950
Impossible.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.740
You’re right.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.350
We’re getting sent away again?

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.790
Where this time?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.990
I don’t know!

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.880
Damn!  Aqua!

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.160
Blue Maiden…

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.690
No good!  I can’t log out!

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.330
How can I log out?

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.680
What will happen to us?

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:14.910
Hayami!

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.880
Use our whole company to rescue Blue Maiden!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.770
How?

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:22.510
By any means possible!

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.620
Hurry!

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.570
Akira.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.930
I know how you feel, but shouldn't 
you be doing something else?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:38.660
You have to save as many people as possible.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:43.580
We can’t have any more people like us.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.020
You're right.  Your brother was also...

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.840
Hayami!  I take back what I said!

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.580
Our priority is to save 
the people in LINK VRAINS!

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.850
Hurry!

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.020
Understood!

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.600
Good job against Blue Maiden.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:14.130
We’ve defeated two so far, 
but we lost Windy and Haru.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.080
We're at a disadvantage.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:24.010
So I want to test an interesting 
plan that won't hurt us.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.980
Playmaker is unexpectedly our secret weapon.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.900
Anger, sadness, grief…

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:38.190
An opponent that'll stir 
up all those emotions.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.900
Damn!  How long will they keep us locked up?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.740
What’s that?

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:02.900
Bohman!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.180
How dare you harm Aqua!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.650
Prepare yourself!  I’ll crush you!

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.690
No.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.780
I didn’t come here to duel you.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:18.140
I came here to say goodbye.

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.300
What?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:28.050
Playmaker, you'll face a 
big test in your next duel.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:34.520
Lightning said emotions 
are humans’ weakness.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:39.190
If we take advantage of 
it, we can win easily.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:45.730
Your next opponent is a terrifying 
foe who'll crush all your emotions.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:48.320
Why are you telling me this?

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.700
Who knows.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:56.670
You served as a model for me.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:02.140
Until today, my goal was 
to defeat you in a duel.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.750
But others can affect my goal.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:11.890
These thoughts stirred my emotions, 
as if a wind blew through me.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.850
Playmaker.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:21.830
If we ever meet again, I'll 
be the one to defeat you.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.520
Fight well.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.460
Fight well?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:32.270
You coward!  Fight me right now!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.250
Damn!

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:41.180
What’s going on with LINK VRAINS?

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.900
Brother…

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.860
Brother…

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.090
Jin!

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.830
Hey, Playmaker.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:57.300
The opponent Bohman mentioned 
- is he super powerful?

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:07.510
What's going on?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:20.390
This is Den City's courtyard.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.540
You arrived.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.030
Brings back memories.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.920
Playmaker.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:35.360
This is where we met for the 
first time in real life.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.580
Ai, this is also where we first met.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:46.370
This is where everything began for us.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:50.240
Kusanagi, we're busy.  Why 
are we talking about this?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.480
And this is LINK VRAINS, right?

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.610
Why are you here?

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.820
The time has finally come.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:58.960
Yeah.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.860
Exactly.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:05.720
Huh?  What’s with both of you?

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:09.510
No way!  Is the opponent Bohman mentioned...

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:16.240
Yes.  You’re dueling me next.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:21.280
Brother, save me.

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:22.350
Jin!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:27.020
Save me.  Come save me.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.860
Handle the rest.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.650
Into the VRAINS!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.750
Welcome, Shoichi Kusanagi.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.950
To our castle of light.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.320
Jin!

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.880
Thanks for coming.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:59.360
Due to Revolver’s program, 
we can’t go to you.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:02.130
Lightning, what do you want with me?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:08.140
Oh my.  You don’t know 
why I called you here.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.130
I didn't expect Playmaker’s 
partner to be so dumb.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.750
I want you to do something.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.200
I won't do it!

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.740
Yes, that is the response I expected.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:26.980
But you can't refuse my request.

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:33.020
See that light?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.690
That's your brother’s real consciousness.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:37.660
What?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:43.470
As long as it's safe, his 
consciousness can be restored.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:47.340
I’m willing to give it back to you.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.560
On one condition.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.570
Condition?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:57.540
Face Playmaker and defeat him.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.050
What?

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.520
It’s your choice.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.520
But a duel is a real battle.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:09.460
If you lose on purpose, I'll erase 
your brother’s consciousness.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.110
I won’t accept a tie either.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:15.400
Defeat Playmaker.  That’s the condition.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:20.170
If I win, you’ll give me back my brother?

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.990
Of course.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:28.340
I have to defeat you, no matter what.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:34.760
Playmaker and Ai…  Lose for Jin!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.220
What should we do, Playmaker?

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.510
You don’t need to show me mercy!

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:46.400
Will you two survive?  Or 
will Jin and I survive?

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.610
Let's fight!

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.840
Huh?  It's Den City!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:03.310
Boss!  We were able to log out!

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:07.330
You fool!  Then why are we in avatar form?

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.650
You’re right.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:11.120
Look!  It’s Playmaker!

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.690
Playmaker is dueling this time.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:19.100
Boss, who’s the opponent?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.560
I don’t know.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:27.010
But if he's showing up now, 
he must be a powerful duelist!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.850
Start broadcasting!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.540
Okay!

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.780
Playmaker!

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:36.680
His opponent is…

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.580
That’s Kusanagi!

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.500
Why is Kusanagi dueling Playmaker?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.220
I can think of only one reason.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.190
They used his brother to blackmail him!

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:53.430
The Light Ignis is using unfair tactics.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:59.860
If Shoichi Kusanagi loses, will 
you really erase the origin?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:05.710
Of course.  He couldn't save 
his best friend’s loved one.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:10.560
That fact will damage Playmaker greatly.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.850
That'll work to our advantage 
in our next fight.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.640
Am I wrong?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.220
Playmaker, what should we do?

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.590
Let’s go, Playmaker!

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.430
Duel!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:30.280
I’ll go first!  My turn!

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.260
I summon Codebreaker Zero Day!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.160
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:47.410
It’s your turn, Playmaker!

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.850
That's Shoichi Kusanagi.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.790
Why is he dueling Playmaker?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.340
Look at this.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:03.540
It's a program to hack Mirror LINK VRAINS.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.530
The sender is Shoichi Kusanagi.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:12.800
I see.  He thought this might 
happen, so he sent us his data.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.800
But it looks unfinished.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:22.800
If we work together, we can 
complete this program quickly.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:25.650
Let’s begin now.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:29.890
We must support Revolver as fast as we can.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.200
Playmaker…

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.640
I know.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.740
It's my turn.  I draw.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.600
I summon Digitron from my hand!

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:51.010
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:55.050
The summoning condition is one monster.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:55.910
Link Summon!

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.620
Link 1 Link Spider!

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.850
Link Spider’s effect!

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:07.330
I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower monster 
from my hand next to this card’s link.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.550
Come, Bitron!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:20.220
When there’s a Cyberse on my field, I can 
Special Summon Backup Secretary from my hand.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:25.550
Appear again!  The circuit 
that leads to the future!

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:28.620
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:30.420
Link Summon!

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:33.720
Link 2 Protocol Gardna!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:39.160
Appear for a third time!  The 
circuit that leads to the future!

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:42.460
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.360
Link Summon!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:49.250
Appear!  Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:53.120
Playmaker, you’re really going to fight?

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:55.740
Decode Talker…

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:59.640
Kusanagi and I acquired this card together.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:01.810
It symbolizes our will to fight.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:24.600
If he summoned Decode Talker so that it 
would link to Zero Day, it would've gained 500 ATK.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:27.460
Is Playmaker unsure if he wants to fight?

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:28.480
Of course!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:33.410
There’s no way he can attack Kusanagi!

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.380
But if he can’t…

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:41.690
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.630
I end my turn.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:54.080
This duel will create a 
giant scar in their hearts.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.000
That’s the goal.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.910
If Shoichi Kusanagi wins, that’s fine.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:04.730
But if Playmaker wins, he'll 
take big damage to his heart.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:09.270
Either way, it's over for Playmaker.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.490
What’s wrong, Playmaker?

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.420
You can’t attack?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.680
But I’m not like you.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:21.360
I will defeat you!

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:27.940
I summon Codebreaker Zero Day!

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:36.950
I activate the Continuous Trap, 
Codebreak Backfire that I already set!

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:42.810
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.820
The summoning conditions 
are two Codebreakers!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.960
Link Summon!

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:56.000
Appear!  Link 2 Codebreaker Virus Swordsman!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.770
Why there?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:04.980
Decode Talker’s effect.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:11.440
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster next to its links.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.030
Power Integration.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:20.890
Why is Kusanagi raising our ATK?

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.060
Here I go, Playmaker and Ai!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.860
Codebreaker Virus Swordsman’s effect!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:31.810
When it's Special Summoned 
so that it’s co-linked...

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:35.280
...I can Special Summon a 
Level 4 or lower Codebreaker

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.570
from my hand or graveyard next 
to your link in defense position.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:43.410
Resurrect, Codebreaker Zero Day!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.340
Virus Backup!

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:51.050
Hey!  He resurrected it on our field?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:55.020
Codebreaker Zero Day’s effect!

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:59.340
Non-Codebreaker Link Monsters 
linked to Zero Day have their

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.990
ATK increases and decreases reversed!

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:04.700
Reversal Force!

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:14.340
It was supposed to gain ATK, 
but it lost them instead!

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:18.250
Codebreak Backfire’s effect!

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:25.250
When a Codebreaker is Special Summoned 
to your field, you take 600 damage!

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.960
Kusanagi!

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.440
Is he serious?

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:43.400
This attack dealt more damage to 
Playmaker than the numbers indicate.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:50.660
Kusanagi!  You’re fine 
with attacking your friend?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:56.590
Ai, it doesn’t matter what you think.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:01.490
This is the only way to save my brother!

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.760
So what!

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:07.060
Playmaker has been fighting 
for you all this time!

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:07.740
But still-

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:12.030
No matter what you say, Jin 
is the most important to me!

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:15.810
Go, Codebreaker Virus Swordsman!

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:18.240
Attack Decode Talker!

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:22.950
Codebreak Backfire’s additional effect!

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:26.540
When it's is in the Spell & Trap Zone...

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:30.650
...Decode Talker isn’t destroyed 
in a battle against a Codebreaker!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.640
Are you okay, Playmaker?

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.360
I’m fine.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:55.710
Kusanagi's gonna pummel us by not letting 
the weakened Decode Talker be destroyed!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.880
Codebreaker Virus Swordsman’s effect!

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:05.080
The battling Decode Talker loses 
500 ATK for every Codebreaker.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:09.090
And you take damage equal to the decrease!

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.090
Hey!  This is bad!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:13.000
Decode Talker’s effect!

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:17.240
When your effect affects 
a monster on my field...

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:23.070
...I can tribute a monster next to its link 
to negate the activation and destroy it!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.940
I tribute Codebreaker Zero Day.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:31.780
Codebreaker Virus Swordsman’s 
effect is negated and destroyed!

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:39.520
Since two Codebreakers are gone, Decode 
Talker’s ATK return to normal!

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:44.040
That was close.  We ended 
up taking minimal damage.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:47.720
And we got rid of two Codebreakers.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.850
It’s too early to feel safe!

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.830
Codebreaker Virus Swordsman’s effect!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:59.840
When your effect destroys it, I can Special 
Summon it from the graveyard at the end of the turn!

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:01.780
What?  That means…

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:05.320
Codebreaker Virus Swordsman’s effect!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.580
Virus Backup!

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:13.040
Codebreaker Zero Day’s effect.

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:21.140
And Codebreak Backfire’s effect!

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:26.930
When a Codebreaker is Special Summoned 
to your field, you take 600 damage!

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:41.060
Playmaker, I know your deck more than anyone.

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:45.260
Sorry, but you’re now going down!

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:50.010
Kusanagi is serious.  What should we do?

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:53.260
I know, but...

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:01.080
I can’t fight Kusanagi.

